condition_name: Acute Peri-Apical Abscess
condition_slug: acute-peri-apical-abscess
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: A localized collection of pus in the peri-apical region of a tooth contained within the alveolar bone.
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical features
    features[4]: Painful swelling at the root of tooth,Sinus (may be present),Tooth is tender to biting or percussion,Tooth may be mobile
investigations[1]: Radiographs (periapical)
treatment:
  goals[2]: Relieve symptoms,Eliminate the infection
  non_drug[3]: Drain abscess using local anaesthesia by root canal extirpation if tooth is to be retained,Otherwise extract the involved tooth,Treat residual infection
  drug[11]: "Amoxicillin - Adult: 250 mg orally every 8 hours for 5 to 7 days","Amoxicillin - Child up to 10 years: 125 mg every 8 hours for 5-7 days, doubled in severe infections","Metronidazole - Adult: 200 mg orally every 8 hours for 3 - 7 days","Metronidazole - 1 - 3 years: 50 mg orally 8 hourly for 3 - 7 days","Metronidazole - 3-7 years: 100 mg 8 hourly","Metronidazole - 7-10 years: 100 mg 8 hourly for 3-7 days","Clindamycin - Adult: 150 - 300 mg every 6 hours; up to 450 mg every 6 hours in severe infections","Clindamycin - Child: 1 month – 18 years 3 - 6 mg/kg (max. 450 mg) every 6 hours",Clindamycin - Neonate Under 14 days 3-6 mg/kg 3 times daily,Clindamycin - Neonate 14-28 days 3-6 mg/kg (max. 450 mg) 4 times daily,"Clindamycin - By deep intramuscular injection or by intravenous infusion, 0.6-2.7 g daily (in 2-4 divided doses) life threatening infection, up to 4.8 g daily; single doses above 600 mg by intravenous infusion only; single doses by intravenous infusion not to exceed 1.2 g"
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[1]: "Discontinue immediately if diarrhoea or colitis develops; monitor liver and renal function if treatment exceeds 10 days, and in neonates and infants; avoid rapid intravenous administration; avoid in acute porphyria"
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[2]: Infected radicular cyst,Periodontal abscess
complications[0]:
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null